sequenceDiagram
  actor U as Optometrist
  participant App as React app
  participant API as FastAPI
  participant Q as Quality check
  participant P as Preprocess
  participant M as DUAL model
  participant C as Calibrator
  participant G as Grad-CAM
  participant DB as Supabase (PostgreSQL + Storage)
  Note over M,G: Sprint 1: mock model and mock heatmaps (real model in Sprint 3)
  U->>App: choose patient and eye, upload photo
  App->>API: POST /images
  API->>Q: check photo quality
  Q-->>API: passed or failed, with reason
  API->>DB: save image and quality status
  alt quality failed
    API-->>App: failed, with reason (for example too dark)
    App-->>U: alert: retake or upload another photo
  else quality passed
    API-->>App: passed
    U->>App: Screen this photo
    App->>API: POST /screenings
    API->>P: preprocess photo
    P->>P: fundus crop or centered-square fallback, 512 x 512
    P->>M: image tensor
    M->>C: raw cataract and glaucoma scores
    C->>C: calibrate, check uncertainty first, then apply disease threshold if confident
    C-->>API: per condition: Refer, No concern or Uncertain, refer
    API->>API: overall for the eye: Refer if any condition is Refer or uncertain
    API->>G: request cataract and glaucoma heatmaps
    G-->>API: heatmaps
    API->>DB: save screening, condition results, heatmaps, model version
    API-->>App: screening result
    App-->>U: Results screen: overall result, one chip per condition, heatmap
  end
